"""mi50 fork: Vega 20 (MI50, PCI 1002:66a1) VBIOS access for AM - design v2 B4 / §6 (egpu/mi50/notes/Vega20 Port Design v2.md).

Vega 20 has no discovery binary the driver needs and macOS never runs the option ROM, so the ATOM data tables Linux reads for
CHIP_VEGA20 (gfx_info -> gc_info, vram_usagebyfirmware -> VRAM reservation, firmwareinfo -> scratch base + bootup clocks,
powerplayinfo -> §6 limits / OverDrive8 ranges / the SMU pptable blob) come from the ROM image read through SMUIO ROM_INDEX/ROM_DATA.
Every struct here is a byte-for-byte port of the cited Linux line (L/ = drivers/gpu/drm/amd of the pinned Linux tree); all tables are
#pragma pack(1) (L/include/atomfirmware.h:214, L/pm/powerplay/hwmgr/vega20_pptable.h:26). Nothing here touches hardware except
read_rom(), and that only through the two register accessors it is given.
"""
